			// Hey! Here is the file containing all the Linux commands I have learned so far. Hope it helps!

:-> pwd: Displays your present/current working directory path.
:-> ls: Lists files and folders.
:-> cd: Changes your current directory.
:-> mkdir: Creates/Make a new direcory.
:-> touch: Creates a blank file.
:-> cat: Displays file content immediately.
:-> cp: Copies files or folders.
:-> mv: Moves or renames files.   //If move in same folder then it rename the file.
:-> rm: Deletes/remove files or folders.
:-> clear: Clears the screen/Terminal.

		//Date commands with flags.
:-> date: Displays current date, time, and timezone.
:-> date -u: Displays time in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).
:-> date -R: Outputs date in RFC-2822 format for emails.
:-> date -I: Shows date in ISO-8601 standard format (YYYY-MM-DD).
:-> date -d "next Friday": Displays the date of the upcoming Friday.
:-> date -d "yesterday": Shows yesterday's exact date and time.
:-> date -d "10 days ago": Calculates the date from 10 days in the past.
:-> date +"%Y-%m-%d": Formats output strictly as Year-Month-Day.
:-> date +"%H:%M:%S": Formats output strictly as Hours:Minutes:Seconds.
:-> date +"%A": Displays only the full current weekday name.


